      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Goal-kicking call",
          "heading": "Kalvin Gourgues expected to take over France's goal-kicking against Argentina",
          "body": "The Toulouse centre is in line for the tee on Saturday, Rugbyrama reports, which would make him France's third goal-kicker in three Nations Championship matches. Thomas Ramos is out with a thigh injury, Romain Ntamack hurt his shoulder against Fiji, scrum-half Maxime Lucu — 3/4 against South Africa — looks bound for the bench and Matthieu Jalibert is being spared kicking after recent right quadriceps trouble. Gourgues landed his only attempt against Fiji; his one other professional stint with the tee brought a perfect 5/5 for Toulouse against Perpignan in January."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat All Blacks 35-28",
