    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Udine week",
          "heading": "Italy schedule children's ward visit and war memorial tribute around Fiji test",
          "body": "The Italian Rugby Federation's programme for Saturday's Fiji test in Udine began with an Azzurri delegation scheduled to visit the paediatric oncology ward at Santa Maria della Misericordia hospital on Wednesday. Friday brings a tribute at the Redipuglia war memorial to Italy's First World War dead and the launch of a pink Gilbert ball promoting breast-cancer prevention, with €10 from each sale going to the Aviano cancer centre. On matchday, federation president Andrea Duodo opens BlackOut, a conference on head injuries."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat All Blacks 35-28",
