    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Exeter banter",
          "heading": "Tom Hooper jokes about lacing Exeter teammate Dafydd Jenkins's coffee before Wales",
          "body": "Wallabies forward Tom Hooper, back from a shoulder injury, is meeting his Exeter Chiefs teammate Dafydd Jenkins for coffee before Saturday's test against Wales. He joked he \"might slip some laxatives in his coffee.\" Jenkins, a Wales forward, matched the Test record of 38 tackles held by France's Thierry Dusautoir in last weekend's 35-28 win over the All Blacks. Hooper reckons he \"might have to run at him 39 times so he can break the record\". Utility back Ben Donaldson promised to keep challenging the line under the Principality Stadium roof."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat All Blacks 35-28",
          "body": "Scotland beat Australia 15-12 in Nations Championship. England name Furbank, Chessum, Atkinson for All Blacks test."
